  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe and Sustainable envirnoment for persons with specific needs in Refugees Camps and Host Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The protection of vulnerable refugee in the camps and host communities in Kigoma region Tanzania have improved through immediate and long-term sustainable interventions</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vulnerable refugees and host community members in Kigoma Region in three refugee camps and 48 villages in 6 districts use and self- manage civil society structure to build intergenerational community cohesion and resiliance, especially in agriculture, and are supported by other trained civil society (NGOs) and government actors at local, regional and national levels who effectively use disaster risk reduction systems, provide integrated and inclusive prsychosocial support and sustainability promote peacful coexistence of refugees and host communities</narrative>
  </description>
